{
  "id": "battle-carnival",
  "name": "Battle Carnival",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "Battle Carnival was the Pokémon Card Game's big official event in Japan from 2011 to 2013: free, day-long festivals at exhibition halls, held in autumn 2011, spring and autumn 2012 and spring 2013. Its main tournament (the Victory Cup, or the World Challenge Tournament in the spring seasons, which carried invitations to the World Championships) was played in three stages. A streak of wins in the Challenge Stage took a player to the Premier Stage, where everyone got mirror holo promos stamped with that season's logo, and the best players there met in a single-elimination Climax Stage. The top three of each league won Victory Cup, the series' trophy card, in a print for their place stamped with the season's name and set in an acrylic shield.\n\nAround the tournament ran side events for every level: an Experience Battle corner for beginners, which gave out jumbo cards, battles against special guests, Gym Leaders and Team Plasma, team battles and, in 2013, PokéCard Points that bought stamped cards. The 2011 spring season was called off after the March 2011 earthquake, and after the spring 2013 Battle Carnival the year-end events were held as Battle Festa.",
    "sources": [
